# =============================================================================
# Trivy accepted-risk exceptions (reviewed 2026-07-05; re-review each sprint).
#
# Every ID below is upgrade-blocked by a pinned major version. The pip-audit
# --ignore-vuln list in .github/workflows/ci.yml covers the same ROOT CAUSES
# (fastapi<0.47 starlette pin, langgraph 0.2 family, websockets ^13, pytest 9)
# but the two scanners' advisory DBs emit different ID sets — do not expect a
# 1:1 ID match; when unblocking a pin, prune BOTH lists.
#
# starlette 0.46.2 — all fixes land in starlette >=0.49.1/1.x, but
# fastapi 0.115 pins starlette <0.47. Unblock = fastapi >=0.139 bump across
# all 4 services (planned follow-up).
CVE-2025-62727
CVE-2026-48818
CVE-2026-54283
#
# langchain-core — CVE-2026-34070 (legacy load_prompt path traversal) is only
# fixed in langchain-core 1.2.22; the 0.3.x line has no fix. The app does not
# use load_prompt. Unblock = LangGraph 1.x migration (planned follow-up).
CVE-2026-34070
#
# langgraph-checkpoint 2.1.2 — fix is in 3.0.0, blocked by langgraph 0.2 pin
# (langgraph <0.3 requires langgraph-checkpoint <3). The app does not enable
# the vulnerable "json" serializer mode. Unblock = LangGraph 1.x migration.
CVE-2025-64439
#
# langsmith 0.8.5 — fix (0.8.18) requires websockets>=15; the voice/WS
# pipeline pins websockets ^13. TracingMiddleware is not enabled (LangSmith
# tracing off). Unblock = websockets 15 bump (planned follow-up).
GHSA-f4xh-w4cj-qxq8
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Added 2026-08-06, when a Trivy step was finally wired into CI and this file
# was consumed for the first time. Everything below was found by that first
# real scan of the built image — it had never been scanned before, so these are
# pre-existing exposures being recorded, not new ones being introduced.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# json_repair 0.59.10 (interview_core only) — DoS via a circular JSON Schema
# `$ref`. Fixed in 0.60.1, and feedback_billing already ships 0.60.1. Held here
# because livekit-agents 1.5.15 hard-pins `json-repair==0.59.10`; bumping it
# makes pip's resolver fail and the image stops building (verified empirically,
# not assumed). Reachability: json_repair is used by livekit-agents to repair
# LLM JSON output, and we never hand it an attacker-supplied JSON *Schema*,
# which is the vulnerable input. Unblock = livekit-agents bump past the pin.
# See the note at services/interview_core/requirements.txt:44.
GHSA-xf7x-x43h-rpqh
#
# Caddy (usr/local/bin/caddy) — 5 HIGH in the vendored Go toolchain and deps of
# the official `caddy:2-alpine` binary we COPY in (Dockerfile:89). We do not
# build Caddy, so there is nothing to bump on our side: the tag already floats
# to the latest 2.x and upstream has not yet rebuilt against a patched Go.
#
# All five are denial-of-service or traversal in code paths our edge config does
# not expose: no gRPC/xDS (grpc), no client-certificate verification
# (crypto/x509), no MIME parsing of untrusted headers beyond what the reverse
# proxy passes through, and `os.Root` is not used. Caddy here terminates TLS and
# proxies to loopback services; it is not a multi-tenant ingress.
#
# Unblock = a `caddy:2-alpine` rebuild on Go >=1.26.5. Re-check each sprint —
# this is the entry most likely to become stale, and a DoS on the edge is a real
# availability risk against the 99.5% NFR even if it is not a data risk.
CVE-2026-56852
GHSA-hrxh-6v49-42gf
CVE-2026-27145
CVE-2026-39822
CVE-2026-42504
